<title>UK: IPAI reports increase in 3rd qtr alumina output.</title>
<headline>IPAI reports increase in 3rd qtr alumina output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) on Thursday reported a year-on-year increase in third quarter 1996 alumina production.</p>
<p>Provisional IPAI figures show that total alumina production in the third was 10.178 million tonnes, up from third quarter 1995 levels of 9.979 million tonnes. This compares with second quarter 1996 alumina production of 10.308 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Alumina (aluminium oxide trihydrate) is mostly used in the production of primary aluminium metal.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
